> 2. Are there other tools I've overlooked that can do this?

Take a look at "man prpasswd" in the section on u_policy.  When this
is set, the file /tcb/bin/pwpolicy is run to check the password.  I
have attached a simple example of how this works.  You will probably
want to write something a little more robust for production work. :-)
This just checks to see that the password doesn't equal the username
and that it is mixed case.
-- 
USmail: Bob Sloane, University of Kansas Computer Center, Lawrence, KS, 66045
E-mail: sloane@ukans.edu http://www.ukans.edu/home/sloane Phone:(785)864-0444

#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

#define UPPERCASE 1
#define LOWERCASE 2
#define NUMERIC   4
#define OTHER     8

main() {
  char func[64];
  char pass[64];
  char user[64];
  int ch;
  int i;
  /*
   * first thing should be a function number. Currently, only "1" is defined
   */
  if ( fgets(func,63,stdin) == 0 )
    exit(0);  /* be generous and allow protocol errors */
  /*
   * Second thing should be the username
   */
  if ( fgets(user,63,stdin) == 0 )
    exit(0);  /* be generous and allow protocol errors */
  /*
   * delete the trailing newline that fgets appends
   */
  if ( user[strlen(user)-1] == '\n' ) user[strlen(user)-1] = '\0';
  /*
   * next should be the password
   */
  if ( fgets(pass,63,stdin) == 0 )
    exit(0);  /* be generous and allow protocol errors */
  /*
   * delete the trailing newline that fgets appends
   */
  if ( pass[strlen(pass)-1] == '\n' ) pass[strlen(pass)-1] = '\0';
  /*
   * Don't allow password == username
   */
  if ( strcmp(user,pass) == 0 )
    exit(1);
  /*
   * Make sure it isn't all the same case or all numeric
   */
  for ( i=ch=0; i < strlen(pass); ++i ) {
    if ( pass[i] >= 'a' && pass[i] <= 'z' )
      ch |= LOWERCASE;
    else if ( pass[i] >= 'A' && pass[i] <= 'Z' )
      ch |= UPPERCASE;
    else if ( pass[i] >= '0' && pass[i] <= '9' )
      ch |= NUMERIC;
    else
      ch |= OTHER;
  }
  /*
   * if password is all upper case, 
   *all lower case or all numeric it fails.
   */
  if ( ch == LOWERCASE || ch == UPPERCASE || ch == NUMERIC )
      exit(1);
  /*
   * password is OK.
   */
  exit(0);
}


