ulimit -a shows what the limits currently are, ulimit -Ha shows what 
they can be increased too.

These hard limits are set within the proc subsystem and can be adjusted 
by entries in sysconfigtab. If there are no entries in your sysconfigtab 
then you are getting the ones built into the kernel.

sysconfig -q proc will show the proc subsystem settings for the running 
kernel.

