"Darren Reed" <avalon@caligula.anu.edu.au> wrote in message
news:3cf8fd28@clarion.carno.net.au...
> How easy is it to get & use Tru64 5.1 media ?  If I buy it on ebay,
> will I need a magic key to unlock it so I can install it that is
> dependant on the hostid or will it just work like Solaris will on
> any sparc box (that's supported) ?

You can instal it, no magic required, but... In order to use your system,
you need the base license, either one of these:

OSF-BASE
UNIX-SERVER
UNIX-WORKSTATION

OSF-BASE comes from "the days of old" (DEC OSF/1) and will work on Tru64
5.1. The later two were introduced around 4.0 branch. I'm not sure what the
difference in functionality is, but there is certainly a different price
attached.

Anyway, any one of these is required. With it, users other than root will be
able to login and the IMPLICT-USER license will be activated. On 4.0 branch
it brings 4 concurent user license, so 4 users will be able to login to your
system at the same time. For a standalone server running only server
processes, this is more than enough.

Nix.




