You can use edauth(8) to look at the user's protected password
database (prpasswd or auth) entry or you can write a program
to get the information with the getespwname(3) routine.

From the prpasswd man page:
  u_unsucchg
      The time in this field is a time_t value that indicates the time of the
      last unsuccessful password change. This field should only be set by
      programs that can be used to change the account password. This field is
      ignored if it is set in a template or in the default database.

One way to translate the time_t value to a readable format is to write
a program that calls the ctime(3) routine.

You could also look into writing a perl script to get and translate
this data.


