Digital Networker is the OEM backup software from Legato 
(http://www.legato.com). An enabler is a proof of license, which has to 
be authorized by Legato to keep networker working after 45 days. This is 
not going to happen with an evaluation enabler.

If your server is not the backup server, you should stop the Networker 
daemons (NSRstartstop stop) and deinstall the software. First determine 
the names of the packages with the command setld -i|grep -i networker, 
then remove those packages with setld -d <package name>.

If you want to use Legato for backup, then:
- purchase an enabler from Legato for server, and if necessary, clients 
and modules, which have to be authorized within 45 days.
- the version of Networker which came with Tru64 is probably old. You 
should at least get 5.5x. You could upgrade Tru64 to version 5.1A. On 
the associated products CD, Networker version 6x is included.

